WEBVTT

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.070
<b>Space Out</b>

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.860
<b>Fluffy fluffy</b>

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.020
<b>Fluffy fluffy</b>

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.780
<b>Fluffy</b>

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.780
<b>Fluffy</b>

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.690
<i>I love that there's so many dogs here.</i>

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:15.870
<i>I wish I could pet them.</i>

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.430
<i>What should I have for dinner?</i>

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.180
<i>Maybe I should go to the 
store on the way home.</i>

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.780
<i>Game a little and go to bed.</i>

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.710
<b>Let's play!</b>

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:27.790
<b>Wham</b>

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.640
<i>He came over here!</i>

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.660
<i>To me?</i>

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.390
Long time no see.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.260
<b>Pass</b>

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.250
Oh, yeah.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.250
He's always so fluffy!

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.280
Eeee!

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.980
<b>#11 
Everyday</b>

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.690
Retying shoelaces that weren't loose

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.200
<i>Let's go home.</i>

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.540
<i>"So, what do you do on your days off?"</i>

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.250
<i>That's a pretty common question.</i>

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.540
<i>They're pretty much like this, 
so there's not much to say.</i>

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:29.000
<i>Sometimes, I'm a little envious 
of people who have exciting lives.</i>

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:29.870
This?

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.450
I got hit by my girlfriend.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.350
<i>Not of this guy, though.</i>

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:34.930
You were hit?

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.950
I met with another girl from school, 
and she thought I was cheating.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.080
I see.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.620
And then yesterday, she dumped me.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.730
Just like that?

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.490
It really didn't last long.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:51.430
<i>Do relationships always go like 
this when you're used to the game?</i>

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.730
So, I have a favor to ask.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:55.440
Come with me to this mixer?

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.350
Nope.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.150
<b>Instant.</b>

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:01.250
Look, I figured it wouldn't be 
so easy to get you to come.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.560
And I get that in this day and age,

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.670
some people aren't interested 
in romantic relationships.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.840
But I think life's more fun if you've 
known the joy of having a girlfriend.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:12.050
I understand where you're coming from,

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.310
but I'm not exactly good at
 approaching women romantically.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.380
You realize you're in your 
second year of college, right?

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.690
"I went to an all-boys school, so 
I'm not good at talking to women"

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:22.960
won't work as an excuse forever.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.510
You're right.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:25.590
Right?

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.620
Getting close to someone 
just takes practice.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.010
So let's go practice.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.080
Hmm.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.070
<b>Stare</b>

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.020
...What?

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:43.400
I feel like there's a lot of girls 
out there who'd like your vibe.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.360
There aren't.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.160
I've never been in a 
relationship with a girl.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.260
Hmm, you think so?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.500
<b>Buzz!</b>

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:50.830
Look

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:52.210
Put 
down

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.130
Did you just think you got a notification?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.030
That was the next person over.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.550
Wh-What?

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.760
If I position you correctly, I'm confident 
that I could make you super popular!

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.480
I never asked you to do that...

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:10.640
<i>In the end...</i>

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.190
<i>I was dragged along.</i>

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.510
All right, next person.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.290
I'm Ichikura Hayate.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.270
I'm in my second year at Karatachi 
University, just like Kurosaki.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.830
It's not really a mixer,

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:22.220
it's more of a drinking party with girls 
from a certain all-girls college!

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.030
The idea is to make friends!

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.890
Pretty sure that's what a mixer is.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.160
You're just there to make the numbers match.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.470
All you need to do is be there.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.240
I'm not quite sure how to feel about that.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.820
<i>He's been trying to convince 
me time and again,</i>

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:36.490
<i>but I figure my life won't 
change if I just wait around.</i>

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:40.460
<i>I told myself, sometimes bold 
measures are good, but...</i>

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.920
<b><i>Sparkle sparkle~</i></b>

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.930
It's so nice to meet you!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:47.390
<b>Sparkle sparkle~</b>

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.710
<i>Yeah, this was a mistake.</i>

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.400
<i>We're of different worlds.</i>

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.130
So you and Kurosaki-kun 
go to the same college?

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.620
That's right!

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.030
That means he's smart, huh?

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:54.720
I mean, not as smart as me, but yeah.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.120
Just kidding!

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:57.860
Okay, next!

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.800
I attend the same school as well,

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.010
but I'm studying over in the law department.

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:06.750
Ichikura-kun, is oolong tea okay?

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.750
Uh, yeah.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.500
I'll have a ginger ale.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.570
A beer for me.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.070
Wish I was twenty.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:15.050
Hey, so Ichikura-kun, what's your type?

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.360
Bubbly girls, hands down.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.540
Nobody asked you, Kurosaki-kun!

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:25.980
<i>Being a college student means having 
the freedom to do what you like.</i>

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.210
Did you do any sports?

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.660
I did volleyball through middle school.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.480
Oh, just like Hayate.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:29.220
<i>I guess some people like to widen their 
social network in a setting like this.</i>

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.220
Oh, really?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.490
Drinks are here.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:31.520
Oh, the beer's for me!

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:34.170
Here's your oolong tea, Ichikura-kun.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.130
Thank you.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:39.120
All right, then let's formally 
toast to getting together tonight!

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:40.190
Cheers!

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.020
<b>Missed it</b>

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:45.980
Speaking of living on your own, your 
apartment's pretty big, huh?

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.060
Oh, really?

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.030
And your rent isn't too bad?

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.660
It belongs to a family friend
 who's abroad for work.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.420
He's letting me stay there
 in the meantime.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.810
I just need to pay the utilities.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.570
Living in Tokyo, though,

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:02.340
you always wonder if you're going 
to bump into someone famous.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.790
You sure do!

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.640
I'm going to the restroom.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:06.270
All right.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.700
But they're more rare than you think.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.590
Yeah, you're right!

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.410
I'm going too.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:12.320
See you soon.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.170
<i>I'm tired.</i>

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:19.240
<i>I don't want to go to the afterparty, 
so maybe I can go home soon.</i>

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.270
Ichikura-kun, are you 
coming to the afterparty?

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.290
No. I'm going home.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.790
Oh. I see.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:36.450
So about your apartment, what's it like?

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.910
Maybe I could go see it...

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.400
It's messy, so now's not a great time.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.830
Oh, of course! I'm really sorry!

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:49.620
<i>Hm, did he not get what I meant?!</i>

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.990
Well then, can you give me your contact 
details so I can come by some other time?

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:57.410
Uh, sure. That's no problem...

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:58.320
<i>All right!</i>

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:00.390
Huh?

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.850
<b>Dead</b>

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:05.240
<i>Huh? I know I charged this 
properly before I left.</i>

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:05.940
Plug

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:06.730
Good.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:07.740
<b>Uh oh</b>

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:08.950
<i>Don't tell me it's broken!</i>

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:11.040
I'm sorry.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:16.540
It looks like my phone is broken, so 
I cannot give you that information.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.590
Looks like Hayate's taking off here.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.400
I kinda dragged him out here tonight.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:22.510
Thanks for coming!

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:23.690
I knew it!

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:26.010
This didn't seem like your kind of scene.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:27.160
Thanks for coming!

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.650
Yes. Thank you.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.630
Bye bye!

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.320
Miki, you going to let him go?

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:33.730
You were so excited about 
him being totally your type.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:34.600
He's leaving.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.110
I know.

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:39.060
But when I asked him for his 
contact details earlier...

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:44.030
He brushed me off with the most transparent 
excuse that his phone was broken!

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:46.600
Ouch. I guess that was a dead end, then.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.780
<b>Cry!</b>

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:52.560
But maybe him blaming his phone 
was his way of being kind.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.870
Hey, what's wrong now?

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.340
Nothing.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.450
<i>I'm tired, but...</i>

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:00.940
Let's take a picture!

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:02.170
That's a great idea!

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:06.120
<i>When you get to talking, 
everyone's actually quite nice.</i>

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:11.840
<b>Party Party Party</b>

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:11.840
<b>Extroverts</b>

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:07.760
Let's go to the next place!

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.030
Go, go!

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.850
<i>There are just times when
 I can't keep up with them.</i>

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.190
<i>But still...</i>

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:19.560
Meow.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.800
<i>Among the days that are not 
worth talking about...</i>

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:30.830
<i>I wonder if it'll work again 
if I plug it back in.</i>

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:31.110
<b>Plug</b>

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:31.110
<b>Plug</b>

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:32.820
<b>Dead...</b>

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:38.660
<b>Plug</b>

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.220
<i>Just another one of my goofs.</i>

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.620
Charging

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.460
<i>It just wasn't charged.</i>

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.160
I'm glad.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.040
<b><i></i>Chat List</b>

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.040
<b>Futami</b>

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.040
<b>New messages received.</b>

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.040
<b>20% OFF when you pay now</b>

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.050
<i>Looks like Shun-kun wrote me.</i>

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:55.730
<i>Sir, I couldn't get 100 points everywhere.</i>

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:55.720
<b>Futami</b>

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:55.720
<b>I couldn't get 100 

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.480
<i>Wow, all these scores are high.</i>

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.700
<i>But he's still bitter about it.</i>

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:01.810
<i>He's so strict with himself.</i>

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:07.300
<i>These rare sparks might be 
the real pleasure in my everyday life.</i>

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.150
I'm proud of you, Shun-kun.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:10.780
<b>Vibrate</b>

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:14.070
<i>I forgot to say.</i>

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:22.040
<b>Futami</b>

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:22.040
<b>I forgot to say</b>

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:22.040
<b>Futami</b>

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:22.040
<b>I have a tournament this weekend,

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:22.040
<b>interested.  Since I haven't been</b>

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:22.040
<b>able to impress you at all.</b>

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:18.010
<i>I have a tournament this weekend, so please 
come watch if you're interested.</i>

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:21.290
<i>Since I haven't been able 
to impress you at all.</i>

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:23.650
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:26.490
<i>He was studying hard for the test so 
he could play in this tournament.</i>

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.590
<i>I'll definitely be there.</i>

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.970
<b>Coming up next</b>

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.970
<b>Progress</b>

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
